      "value": "The hypothesis claims N_c(w) should be flat (rigid solution space) given prior iteration 20, but the current system reports a surprise score of 1.0 (worst case), indicating the prediction failed. This suggests the underlying mathematical structure may not be rigid as assumed. I will explore the design space by re-evaluating the constraint family construction and testing alternative hypotheses using the capacity_scan pipeline with varied constraint families (rigid vs. fat) to determine whether the solution space is truly dimension-0 or higher-dimensional. This involves systematically testing different constraint families to see if N_c(w) remains flat or increases with w, thereby validating or refuting the rigidity hypothesis."
